{"id":"book-iv-translator-and-historical-edition-notes","label":"Against Heresies: Book IV — Translator and historical edition notes","headingNoteRefs":"","context":"Against Heresies: Book IV","kind":"commentary","blocks":[{"text":"[^irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-1]: [The reader who marvels at the tedious recitals must note this (1) as proof of the author’s practical wisdom, and (2) as evidence of his fidelity in what he exhibits.]","kind":"commentary","noteId":"irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-1"},{"text":"[^irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-2]: Luke i. 2 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-2"},{"text":"[^irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-3]: 2 Tim. ii. 23 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-3"},{"text":"[^irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-4]: [The solemnity of the apostolic testimonies against the crop of tares that was to spring up receives great illustration from Irenæus. 1 John ii. 18 .]","kind":"commentary","noteId":"irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-4"},{"text":"[^irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-5]: [ 2 Pet. ii. 19 .]","kind":"commentary","noteId":"irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-5"},{"text":"[^irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-6]: [ Rev. xii. 9 . A little essay, Messias and Anti-Messias , by the Rev. C. I. Black, London (Masters, 1847), is commended to those who need light on this very mysterious subject.]","kind":"commentary","noteId":"irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-6"},{"text":"[^irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-7]: Gen. i. 26 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-7"},{"text":"[^irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-8]: See iii. 6, 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-8"},{"text":"[^irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-9]: [St. John xvii. 3 .]","kind":"commentary","noteId":"irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-9"},{"text":"[^irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-10]: Matt. xxiii. 9 .","kind":"commentary","noteId":"irenaeus-against-heresies-ix-vi-10"},{"text":"[^irenaeus-agai